# Tauri 2 + Rust bridge

Canon: ADR-0042, `apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/default.json`.

## Must

- Keep capabilities least-privilege. Default is `core:default` plus
  `dialog:allow-open`. Do not add FS, shell, or HTTP plugins without an ADR.
- Every `#[tauri::command]` stays on an explicit `invoke_handler` allowlist.
- Foundation/inception/workspace methods stay on the existing method match
  lists. New RPC needs a new arm, not a wildcard.
- Rust owns windows, folder dialogs, daemon child lifecycle, socket/pipe
  transport, and cleanup.
- CSP stays `default-src 'self'` (plus the documented img/style/script self
  exceptions). No remote origins.

## Must not

- Implement inspect, doctor, apply, feature-intent, or bounded-execution
  rules in Rust.
- Expose a generic filesystem, shell, or network bridge to the webview.
- Hand-edit `src-tauri/gen/` or commit `target/`.
- Grow `main.rs` further; extract transport vs allowlist vs lifecycle on the
  next meaningful change.
